# An agent stopped on the menu its question tool draws, at 24 columns, as
# claude 2.1.259 draws it. The box's height is the agent's own choice, and two
# one-sentence descriptions are enough to push its top past the rows a rule may
# see: the marker on the first choice scrolls away while the whole bottom of
# the box stays. The footer wraps in three at this width, which leaves
# `Enter to select` on the row it opens and breaks `Esc to cancel` in half.
print ────────────────────────
print  ☐ Indentation
print
print Should this project be
print indented with spaces or
print tabs?
print
print ❯ 1. Spaces
print      Fixed-width
print      indentation that
print      renders identically
print      everywhere; the
print      common default for
print      most language style
print      guides and
print      formatters.
print   2. Tabs
print      One tab character
print      per level, so each
print      reader's editor
print      controls the
print      visible width;
print      better for
print      accessibility and
print      smaller files.
print   3. Type something.
print ────────────────────────
print   4. Chat about this
print
print Enter to select · ↑/↓ to
print navigate · Esc to
print cancel
# The menu waits for an answer, and nothing else ends it.
sleep 600000
